2
00:08:10,434 --> 00:08:16,434
The Babadook is a drama, horror film directed by Jennifer Kent.

3
00:12:15,652 --> 00:12:21,652
A single mother, plagued by the violent death of her husband, battles with her son's fear of a
monster lurking in the house, but soon discovers a sinister presence all around her.

4
00:16:20,869 --> 00:16:26,869
Amelia Vanek, played by Essie Davis.

5
00:20:26,086 --> 00:20:32,086
Samuel Vanek, played by Noah Wiseman.

6
00:24:31,304 --> 00:24:37,304
Claire, played by Hayley McElhinney.

7
00:28:36,521 --> 00:28:42,521
Robbie, played by Daniel Henshall.

8
00:32:41,739 --> 00:32:47,739
Gracie Roach, played by Barbara West.

9
00:36:46,956 --> 00:36:52,956
Oskar Vanek, played by Ben Winspear.

10
00:40:52,173 --> 00:40:58,173
The Babadook is a 2014 Australian psychological horror film written and directed by Jennifer
Kent in her feature directorial debut, based on her 2005 short film Monster.

11
00:44:57,391 --> 00:45:03,391
Starring Essie Davis, Noah Wiseman, Daniel Henshall, Hayley McElhinney, Barbara West, and Ben Winspear, the film follows
a widowed single mother who, with her son, must confront a mysterious humanoid monster in their home.

12
00:49:02,608 --> 00:49:08,608
Kent began writing the screenplay in 2009, intending to
explore parenting, grief, and the fear of madness.

13
00:53:07,826 --> 00:53:13,826
Financing was secured through Australian government
grants and partly through crowdfunding.

14
00:57:13,043 --> 00:57:19,043
Filming took place in Adelaide, where Kent drew from her experiences as a
production assistant on Lars von Trier's Dogville (2003).

15
01:01:18,260 --> 01:01:24,260
During filming, the production team worked to ensure six-year-old Wiseman
was protected from the film's disturbing subject matter.

16
01:05:23,478 --> 01:05:29,478
The Babadook premiered at the Sundance Film Festival on 17 January 2014 and was given a limited release in
Australian cinemas on 22 May 2014, initially failing to become a commercial success in its native country.

17
01:09:28,695 --> 01:09:34,695
However, it generated wider attention internationally,
grossing $10 million against its $2 million budget.

18
01:13:33,913 --> 01:13:39,913
The film was praised for the cast's performances,
creature design, premise, and themes.

19
01:17:39,130 --> 01:17:45,130
At the 4th AACTA Awards, it won for Best Film, and Kent won for Best
Direction and Best Original Screenplay, respectively.

20
01:21:44,347 --> 01:21:50,347
In the years since its release, The Babadook has become a cult classic.

21
01:25:49,565 --> 01:25:55,565
The film explores themes of monster, nightmare, parent child
relationship, dysfunctional family, sleeplessness.

22
01:29:54,782 --> 01:30:00,782
The tone is lighthearted and dark and emotional.
